<body>
<div class="page">
  <div class="header-section">
    <h1 style="font-size: 20pt;">Francis Marion University – Quote Request</h1>
    <p>Quote Name and Number: <span data-field="quote_name_number">{{ quote_name_number }}</span> – <span data-field="quote_description">{{ quote_description }}</span></p>
    <p>Date: <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span></p>
    <p>Francis Marion University is accepting quotes for a contractor to print and deliver FMU Academic Catalogs as described herein.</p>
    <p>The following schedule is required to be completed by the offeror:</p>
    <p>Please quote your lowest delivered price for the item(s) below. Francis Marion University reserves the right to reject any or all quotes and to waive any or all technicalities.</p>
    <p>Notes:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Exclude Sales Tax in your bid prices.</li>
      <li>Include freight/shipping. FOB Destination included to Florence, SC.</li>
      <li>The attached Terms and Conditions apply to all quotes and supersedes Offeror's Terms and Conditions.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Item Details</div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Item</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Quantity</th>
        <th style="width: 50%;">Description</th>
        <th style="width: 15%; text-align: right;">Unit Price</th>
        <th style="width: 15%; text-align: right;">Total Price</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in line_items %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ loop.index }}</td>
        <td><span data-field="line_items[{{ loop.index0 }}].quantity">{{ item.quantity }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="line_items[{{ loop.index0 }}].description">{{ item.description }}</span></td>
        <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="line_items[{{ loop.index0 }}].unit_price">{{ item.unit_price }}</span></td>
        <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="line_items[{{ loop.index0 }}].total_price">{{ item.total_price }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Total Price (excluding sales tax): <span data-field="total_price_excluding_tax">{{ total_price_excluding_tax }}</span></p>

  <div class="section-title">Optional Costs</div>
  <p>Optional costs will be used to adjust the cost for changes to specifications. All items marked must be filled out or bid may be rejected for being non-responsive.</p>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 50%;">Cost per <span data-field="optional_cost_1_quantity">{{ optional_cost_1_quantity }}</span> additional quantities at pressrun</td>
      <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="optional_cost_1_price">{{ optional_cost_1_price }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Cost per <span data-field="optional_cost_2_quantity">{{ optional_cost_2_quantity }}</span> additional quantities within 6 months after press run</td>
      <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="optional_cost_2_price">{{ optional_cost_2_price }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <p>Cost per signature to: <span data-field="cost_per_signature">{{ cost_per_signature }}</span></p>
  <p>Delete <span data-field="delete_signature_count">{{ delete_signature_count }}</span> page signature $ <span data-field="delete_signature_price">{{ delete_signature_price }}</span></p>

  <div class="section-title">Vendor's Best Delivery Date: <span data-field="vendor_best_delivery_date">{{ vendor_best_delivery_date }}</span></div>
  <div class="section-title">Days After Receipt of Order: <span data-field="days_after_receipt_of_order">{{ days_after_receipt_of_order }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">Delivery/Performance Location – Specified Jan 2006: After award, all deliveries shall be made and all services provided to the following address, unless otherwise specified:</div>
  <p>Francis Marion University</p>
  <p><span data-field="delivery_address_street">{{ delivery_address_street }}</span></p>
  <p><span data-field="delivery_address_city_state_zip">{{ delivery_address_city_state_zip }}</span></p>

  <div class="section-title">Quote may be e-mailed to: <span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span> or faxed to <span data-field="fax_number">{{ fax_number }}</span></div>
  <div class="section-title">Quote must be received by: <span data-field="submission_deadline_date">{{ submission_deadline_date }}</span> at <span data-field="submission_deadline_time">{{ submission_deadline_time }}</span></div>
  <p>This section must be completed by the Vendor:</p>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 20%;">Company Name:</td>
      <td><span data-field="company_name">{{ company_name }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Authorized Signature:</td>
      <td><span data-field="authorized_signature">{{ authorized_signature }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Authorized Signature (printed):</td>
      <td><span data-field="authorized_signature_printed">{{ authorized_signature_printed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Date:</td>
      <td><span data-field="date_signed">{{ date_signed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Address:</td>
      <td><span data-field="address_signed">{{ address_signed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>City/State/Zip:</td>
      <td><span data-field="city_state_zip_signed">{{ city_state_zip_signed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Phone Number:</td>
      <td><span data-field="phone_number_signed">{{ phone_number_signed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Fax Number:</td>
      <td><span data-field="fax_number_signed">{{ fax_number_signed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>E-Mail:</td>
      <td><span data-field="email_signed">{{ email_signed }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Federal ID Number:</td>
      <td><span data-field="federal_id_number">{{ federal_id_number }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SC Minority Cert. # (if applicable):</td>
      <td><span data-field="sc_minority_cert_number">{{ sc_minority_cert_number }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">I. SCOPE OF SOLICITATION</div>
  <p>ACQUIRE SERVICES & SUPPLIES / EQUIPMENT (JAN 2006): The purpose of this solicitation is to acquire services and supplies or equipment complying with the enclosed description and/or specifications and conditions. [01-1005-1]</p>

  <div class="section-title">II. INSTRUCTIONS TO OFFERORS – A. GENERAL INSTRUCTIONS</div>
  <p>AMENDMENTS TO SOLICITATION (JAN 2004): (a) The Solicitation may be amended at any time prior to opening. All actual and prospective Offerors should monitor the following web site for the issuance of Amendments: <span data-field="amendment_website_url">{{ amendment_website_url }}</span> (b) Offerors shall acknowledge receipt of any amendment to this Solicitation by signing and returning the amendment. (c) By identifying the amendment, the Offeror shall acknowledge that the amendment is incorporated into the Solicitation. (d) If the amendment is not acknowledged, it shall be deemed that the amendment is not incorporated.</p>
  <p>AUTHORIZED AGENT (FEB 2015): All authority regarding this procurement is vested solely with the responsible Procurement Officer. Unless specifically delegated in writing, the Procurement Officer is the only government official authorized to bind the government with regard to this procurement or the resulting contract. [02-2A007-1]</p>

  <div class="section-title">BID IN ENGLISH & DOLLARS (JAN 2004): Offers submitted in response to this solicitation shall be in the English language and in US dollars, unless otherwise permitted by the Solicitation. [02-2A025-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">AUTHORITY AS PROCUREMENT AGENT (DEC 2015): The Procurement Officer is an employee of the Authority acting on behalf of the Using Governmental Unit(s) pursuant to the Consolidated Procurement Code. Any contracts awarded as a result of this procurement are between the Contractor and the Using Governmental Unit(s). The Authority is not a party to such contracts, unless and to the extent that the Authority is a using governmental unit, and bears no liability for any party's losses arising out of or relating in any way to the contract. [02-2A030-3]</div>

  <div class="section-title">CERTIFICATE OF INDEPENDENT PRICE DETERMINATION (MAY 2008): GIVING FALSE, MISLEADING, OR INCOMPLETE INFORMATION ON THIS CERTIFICATION MAY render YOU SUBJECT TO PROSECUTION UNDER SECTION 16-10 OF THE SOUTH CAROLINA CODE OF LAWS AND OTHER APPLICABLE LAWS. (a) By submitting an offer, the offeror certifies that the information contained in this certification is true and correct. (b) The offeror understands that the submission of a false or misleading statement, representation, or certification may result in the rejection of the offer, termination of the contract, or other legal action.</div>

  <div class="section-title">Disclaimer of Liability</div>
  <p>The solicitation and all related documents are provided for informational purposes only. The Authority makes no warranty or representation as to the accuracy or completeness of the information contained herein. The Authority shall not be liable for any errors or omissions in the Solicitation or any resulting damages.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">Disclaimer of Liability (Continued)</div>
  <p>The Authority reserves the right to modify, amend, or cancel this Solicitation at any time without notice. Any modifications or amendments will be made available to all interested parties through the official procurement website.</p>

  <div class="section-title">RESPONSIBILITY REQUIREMENTS</div>
  <p>(a) The Contractor shall be responsible for all costs and expenses associated with the performance of the contract, including but not limited to labor, materials, equipment, travel, and overhead. (b) The Contractor shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws, regulations, rules, and ordinances. (c) The Contractor shall maintain adequate insurance coverage as required by the contract.</div>

  <div class="section-title">LICENSES, PERMITS, & INSURANCE (FMU – APR 2022): All costs for required licenses, permits and insurance shall be borne by the Contractor.</div>

  <div class="section-title">OFFERING BY LOT (JAN 2006): Offers may be submitted for one or more complete lots. Failure to offer on all items within a lot will be reason for rejection. [02-2B095-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">PROTEST – CPO – MMO ADDRESS (JUN 2006): Any protest must be addressed to the Chief Procurement Officer, Materials Management, and submitted in writing.</div>
  <p>Chief Procurement Officer</p>
  <p>Materials Management</p>
  <p>Francis Marion University</p>
  <p><span data-field="cpo_address_street">{{ cpo_address_street }}</span></p>
  <p><span data-field="cpo_address_city_state_zip">{{ cpo_address_city_state_zip }}</span></p>
  <p>(b) by mail or delivery to 1201 Main Street, Suite 600, Columbia, SC 29201. [02-2B122-1]</p>

  <div class="section-title">QUALIFIED PRODUCTS LIST (JAN 2006): Only products that are on the qualified products list. [02-2B125-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">UNIT PRICES REQUIRED (JAN 2006): Unit price to be shown for each item. [02-2B170-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">COMPLIANCE (FMU – APR 2022): Francis Marion University requires all contractual activities to be performed in a manner that is consistent with all applicable federal, state and local laws, regulations, rules and ordinances. These include, but are not limited to: Occupational Safety and Health Act, The Environmental Protection Act, The South Carolina Hazardous Waste Management Act.</div>

  <div class="section-title">NOTE – IMPORTANT (FMU – APR 2022): Contractors, we MUST have your Federal ID (#) (company) or Social Security # (individual) before processing any invoices for payment. Failure to provide this information will result in delay of payments until this information is received. Please include this information with your quote – see Attachment #2.</div>

  <div class="section-title">III. SCOPE OF WORK / SPECIFICATIONS</div>
  <p>PRINTING MANUAL (JAN 2006): The South Carolina Government Printing Services manual, dated January 1, 1998, governs both the procurement and any resulting contract and is hereby incorporated by reference. You are responsible for obtaining a copy of the manual. The manual is available at <span data-field="printing_manual_url">{{ printing_manual_url }}</span>.</p>
  <p>Contractor must follow the additional specifications listed on the "State of S.C. Printing Specification Sheet" (see Attachment #3).</p>
  <p>NOTE: In the additional specifications listed on the State of S.C. Printing Specification Sheet, the flat size is 16.5" by 10.75", except for the cover, which is 17" by 10.75" to allow for the spine on the perfect bound product. The finished size is 8.25" by 10.75".</p>

  <div class="section-title">Overrun/Underrun: Exact count requested with no underage; overages exceeding 200 will not be accepted.</div>

  <div class="section-title">Contractor Liaison: Contractor shall establish a contract liaison to conference with University personnel to ensure complete understanding of all requirements.</div>
  <p>Note: Contractor shall be responsible for the cost of and transportation of all copy and proofs, including overnight delivery charges.</p>

  <div class="section-title">Liquidated Damages: Contractor to be assessed $100.00 per day to be deducted from the final invoice if product is not received by the established delivery date.</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">Note Regarding Alternate Stock: Alternate stock may be bid for consideration as an "equal", but if an alternate stock is bid, a sample of the product must be included in your quote package. The University will make final determination as to the equality of substitutes offered. Our preference is for stock as specified.</div>

  <div class="section-title">Delivery / Performance Location – Specified Jan 2006: After award, all deliveries shall be made and all services provided to the following address, unless otherwise specified:</div>
  <p>Francis Marion University</p>
  <p>Central Receiving</p>
  <p><span data-field="delivery_address_street_2">{{ delivery_address_street_2 }}</span></p>
  <p><span data-field="delivery_address_city_state_zip_2">{{ delivery_address_city_state_zip_2 }}</span></p>

  <div class="section-title">Delivery Contact:</div>
  <p>Vendor should coordinate all deliveries with Tori Payne at 843-661-1270.</p>

  <div class="section-title">Contract Administration: Questions or problems arising after award of this contract shall be directed to:</div>
  <p>Tori Payne</p>
  <p>Design Project Coordinator</p>
  <p>(843) 661-1270</p>
  <p>Tori.payne@fman.edu</p>
  <p>OR</p>
  <p>FMU Purchasing Office</p>
  <p>Stokes Admin. Building, Ste. 102</p>
  <p>Phone: (843) 661-1160</p>

  <div class="section-title">IV. AWARD CRITERIA – BIDS (JAN 2006): Award will be made to the lowest responsible and responsive bidder(s). [06-6020-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">AWARD TO ONE OFFEROR (JAN 2006): Award will be made to one Offeror. [06-6040-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">DISCUSSIONS AND NEGOTIATIONS – OPTIONAL (FEB 2015): Submit your best terms from both a price and a technical standpoint. Your proposal may be evaluated and your offer accepted without any discussions, negotiations, or prior notice. Ordinarily, the Authority reserves the right to reject any or all offers, waive any or all technicalities, and to award the contract to the bidder whose proposal is deemed to be the best value to the Authority. The Authority reserves the right to negotiate with any or all bidders.</div>

  <div class="section-title">QUALITY – NEW (JAN 2006): All items must be new. [03-3060-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">UNIT PRICE GOVERNS (JAN 2006): In determining award, unit prices will govern over extended prices unless otherwise stated. [06-6075-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">V. TERMS AND CONDITIONS – A. GENERAL</div>
  <p>ASSIGNMENT, NOVATION, AND CHANGE OF NAME, IDENTITY, OR STRUCTURE (FEB 2015): (a) Contractor shall not assign this contract, or its rights, obligations, or any other interest arising from this contract, or delegate any of its performance obligations, without the express written consent of the responsible Procurement Officer. The foregoing restriction does not apply to a transfer that is a result of a merger, consolidation, or sale of substantially all of the assets of the Contractor. (b) The Contractor shall not change its name, identity, or structure without the express written consent of the responsible Procurement Officer. [02-2A025-1]</p>

  <div class="section-title">BANKRUPTCY – GENERAL (FEB 2015): (a) Notice. In the event the Contractor enters into proceedings relating to bankruptcy, whether voluntary or involuntary, the Contractor agrees to furnish written notification of the bankruptcy to the Using Governmental Unit. This notification shall be furnished within two (2) days of the initiation of the proceedings relating to the bankruptcy filing.</div>

  <div class="section-title">CHOICE-OF-LAW (JAN 2006): The Agreement, any dispute, claim, or controversy relating to the Agreement, and all the rights and obligations of the parties shall be interpreted, construed, enforced, and governed by and under the laws of the State of South Carolina, excluding its conflict of laws rules.</div>

  <div class="section-title">CONTRACT DOCUMENTS & ORDER OF PRECEDENCE (FEB 2015): (a) Any contract resulting from this solicitation shall consist of the following documents, in the order of precedence listed below: (1) This Solicitation; (2) Any amendments to this Solicitation; (3) The State of S.C. Printing Specification Sheet (Attachment #3); (4) The Agreement; and (5) Any other documents incorporated by reference. In the event of a conflict between any of these documents, the document listed first in this order of precedence shall govern. (b) Any document signed or otherwise agreed to by persons other than the Procurement Officer shall be void and of no effect. [02-2A015-2]</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">DISPUTES (JAN 2006): (1) Choice-of-Forum. All disputes, claims, or controversies relating to the Agreement shall be resolved exclusively in the state or federal courts located in the State of South Carolina. (2) Venue. The venue for any such action shall be in the State of South Carolina. [07-7A015-2]</div>

  <div class="section-title">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY (JAN 2006): Contractor is referred to and shall comply with all applicable provisions, if any, of Title 41, Part 1, of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended. Contractor shall not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, or any other protected characteristic.</div>

  <div class="section-title">FALSE CLAIMS (JAN 2006): According to the S.C. Code of Laws Section 16-13-240, "a person who by false premise or representation obtains the property of another by fraud or deceit shall be guilty of a crime." The Contractor warrants that all claims submitted are true and correct. [07-7A035-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">FIXED PRICING REQUIRED (JAN 2006): Any pricing provided by contractor shall include all costs for performing the work, including all labor, materials, equipment, overhead, profit, taxes, and all other charges. No additional costs shall be incurred by the Authority. [07-7A040-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">NO INDEMNITY OR DEFENSE (FEB 2015): Any term or condition is void to the extent it requires the State to indemnify, defend, or hold harmless the Contractor. [02-2A025-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">NOTICE (JAN 2006): (a) After award, any notices shall be in writing and shall be deemed duly given upon actual delivery, if delivery by hand, facsimile, electronic mail, or mail (if postmarked on the date of mailing) or upon receipt, if received and registered or certified mail is used. (b) Notice to contractor shall be to the address identified as the Contractor's address in the bid proposal. (c) The Authority reserves the right to send notices to any other address it deems appropriate. [07-7A050-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">OPEN TRADE (JUN 2015): During the contract term, including any renewals or extensions, Contractor will not engage in the boycott of any person or entity based on race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other protected characteristic. [07-7A055-1]</div>

  <div class="section-title">PAYMENT & INTEREST (FEB 2021): (a) The State shall pay the Contractor, after the submission of proper invoices or vouchers, the prices stipulated in this contract for supplies delivered and accepted or services rendered and accepted, less any deductions authorized by the contract. (b) The State shall pay interest on any amounts due to the Contractor that are not paid within the time period specified in the contract, at the rate of one percent (1%) per month or the maximum rate permitted by law, whichever is less.</div>
</div>

